    <bpmn:process id="W_W3761" name="W3761. Employer Brand Strategy, Positioning &amp; EVP Development" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Annual TA planning (links to VS-33.1); EVP refresh; brand-health decline
Frequency: Annual + on change
Volume: Enterprise employer brand &amp; EVP
Owner: TA Marketing / Employer Brand Lead
Participants: TA Marketing, CHRO/HR (links to VS-19/VS-103), Marketing/Brand (links to VS-14.3), Store Ops (links to VS-07), Comms (links to VS-14.3), DEI (links to VS-103.2/W719), Finance (links to VS-17.4)
Source: workflow W3761 — Employer Brand Strategy, Positioning &amp; EVP Development</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3761_LaneSet3">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3761_Lane1" name="TA Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3761_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3761_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3761_Start4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W3761_Lane2" name="CHRO">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3761_Task7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3761_End8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3761_Start4" name="Annual TA planning (links to VS-33.1); EVP refresh; brand-health decline">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3761_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3761_Task5" name="TA Marketing/CHRO define the employer brand strategy and employee value…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: TA Marketing/CHRO define the employer brand strategy and employee value proposition (EVP): research-based positioning ( BuildRight as the Filipino home-building partner and a builder of careers — trade mastery, stability, growth, family orientation), the EVP pillars (pay &amp; benefits links to VS-102, learning &amp; career links to VS-19.4, purpose/impact links to VS-25, culture links to VS-103.2), target talent segments (store frontline, trade-knowledgeable, DC/logistics, corporate/digital), and the brand promise to candidates
Responsible (R): TA Marketing / CHRO
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3761_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3761_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3761_Task6" name="TA Marketing/Brand operationalize the EVP into messaging, visual identity, and…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: TA Marketing/Brand operationalize the EVP into messaging, visual identity, and proof points (real employee stories, career-path examples, recognition links to W630/W973), and align it to the consumer/corporate brand (links to VS-14.3) so the employer brand is consistent across career site, social, store, and external communications
Responsible (R): TA Marketing / Brand
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Annual + ongoing</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3761_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3761_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3761_Task7" name="CHRO/Executive ratify the employer brand strategy and EVP, approve the…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: CHRO/Executive ratify the employer brand strategy and EVP, approve the talent-marketing budget envelope (links to W3768), and cascade the EVP to all hiring managers and recruiters as the standard candidate value proposition
Responsible (R): CHRO / TA Marketing
Accountable (A): CEO
Duration: Annual</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3761_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3761_Flow14</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3761_End8" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3761_Flow14</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3761_Annotation9">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-592 (ensure controlled execution — Employer Brand, EVP &amp; Talent Marketing Strategy (PA-121.1).) | - operational: research-based, segment-specific positioning; operational: proof-point validation and EX alignment (links to VS-103)
Owner: TA Marketing / Employer Brand Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W3761_Assoc10" sourceRef="W3761_Annotation9" targetRef="W3761_Start4" associationDirection="None" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3761_Flow11" sourceRef="W3761_Start4" targetRef="W3761_Task5" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3761_Flow12" sourceRef="W3761_Task5" targetRef="W3761_Task6" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3761_Flow13" sourceRef="W3761_Task6" targetRef="W3761_Task7" />
      <bpmn:sequenceFlow id="W3761_Flow14" sourceRef="W3761_Task7" targetRef="W3761_End8" />
    </bpmn:process>
