    <bpmn:process id="W_W3764" name="W3764. Social Recruiting, Employer Review-Site &amp; Online Reputation Management" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Continuous; review/mention alert; campaign
Frequency: Continuous
Volume: Enterprise social/reputation footprint
Owner: TA Marketing / Comms
Participants: TA Marketing, Comms (links to VS-14.3), Legal (links to VS-100.3), HR (links to VS-103), Store Ops (links to VS-07), IT/Social (links to VS-27)
Source: workflow W3764 — Social Recruiting, Employer Review-Site &amp; Online Reputation Management</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3764_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3764_Lane1" name="TA Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3764_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3764_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3764_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3764_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3764_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3764_Start3" name="Continuous; review/mention alert; campaign">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3764_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3764_Task4" name="TA Marketing/Comms operate social recruiting (Facebook, LinkedIn, TikTok…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: TA Marketing/Comms operate social recruiting (Facebook, LinkedIn, TikTok, Instagram — the channels Philippine candidates use): content calendar showcasing BuildRight as an employer, employee takeovers, behind-the-scenes store/DC content, open-role spotlighting, and community engagement; integrate to career site (W3762)
Responsible (R): TA Marketing / Comms
Accountable (A): TA Marketing Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3764_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3764_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3764_Task5" name="TA Marketing/Comms monitor and manage employer-review sites and online…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: TA Marketing/Comms monitor and manage employer-review sites and online reputation (Glassdoor-equivalent, JobStreet, Google/Facebook reviews, social mentions): monitor sentiment, respond per policy, route actionable feedback to HR/EX (links to VS-103.2) and to specific cases (links to VS-119 speak-up if warranted), and manage coordinated response to negative episodes with Comms/Legal (links to VS-14.3/VS-100.3)
Responsible (R): TA Marketing / Comms / Legal
Accountable (A): TA Marketing Lead
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3764_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3764_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3764_Task6" name="TA Marketing/Analytics report social-recruiting and reputation performance…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: TA Marketing/Analytics report social-recruiting and reputation performance (reach, engagement, sentiment, review rating trend, review-volume) to TA governance (links to W3784) and CHRO, and drive improvement actions
Responsible (R): TA Marketing / Analytics
Accountable (A): TA Marketing Lead
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3764_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3764_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3764_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3764_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W3764_Annotation8">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-592 (ensure controlled execution — Employer Brand, EVP &amp; Talent Marketing Strategy (PA-121.1).) | - operational: monitoring + response policy; operational: Comms/Legal review of sensitive responses
Owner: TA Marketing / Comms</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
