    <bpmn:process id="W_W5557" name="W5557. Recruitment Fraud &amp; Fake Job-Offer Scam Response, Takedown &amp; Victim-Guidance Protocol" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Discovery of a scam impersonating BuildRight recruitment — fake job offers, &quot;training fee&quot; / &quot;processing fee&quot; demands, fake onboarding portals or hiring group chats using the company name, logo, or careers-site look-alikes — reported by victims, employees, or channel monitoring
Frequency: A social-era integrity event that arrives in bursts: a few episodes per year, each clustering dozens to hundreds of victim contacts around a single fake hiring campaign
Volume: 1 campaign × the victim surface (10–500 contacts) × the takedown surfaces (social pages and group chats, look-alike domains, SMS/e-mail blasts) × the response desk (TA Marketing, IP Counsel, the store-facing script)
Owner: TA Marketing / Employer Brand Lead
Participants: IP Counsel (W3272 takedown machinery), Corporate Communications (W134 advisory; W143 media), Corporate Security (VS-159 threat intake), IT Security (phishing-domain coordination, VS-27.3), Store Managers and HR front desk (walk-in victim script), Talent Acquisition Operations (offer-verification registry, W3762), Data Protection Officer (VS-91 if harvested personal data surfaces), PNP Anti-Cybercrime Group
Source: workflow W5557 — Recruitment Fraud &amp; Fake Job-Offer Scam Response, Takedown &amp; Victim-Guidance Protocol</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W5557_LaneSet6">
        <bpmn:lane id="W5557_Lane1" name="TA Marketing">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5557_Task8</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5557_Task11</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5557_Task12</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5557_Task15</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5557_Start7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5557_Lane2" name="Corporate Communications">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5557_Task9</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5557_Lane3" name="IP Counsel">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5557_Task10</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5557_Lane4" name="Corporate Security">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5557_Task13</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
        <bpmn:lane id="W5557_Lane5" name="Talent Acquisition Operations">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5557_Task14</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W5557_End16</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W5557_Start7" name="Discovery of a scam impersonating BuildRight recruitment — fake job offers, &quot;training…">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5557_Flow19</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5557_Task8" name="Report intake &amp; evidence capture">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Report intake &amp; evidence capture: screenshots, URLs, sender numbers, payment channels, and any fake offer letters preserved to the case; victim reports logged with contact consent for follow-up
Responsible (R): TA Marketing / HR Front Desk / Corporate Security
Accountable (A): TA Marketing / Employer Brand Lead
Duration: Same day</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5557_Flow19</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5557_Flow20</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5557_Task9" name="Same-day scam advisory publication">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Same-day scam advisory publication: careers-site banner (W3762) plus official social channels and the W3764 monitoring surfaces: BuildRight never charges application, training, or processing fees; no offer is valid unless it appears in the official candidate portal; only official channels announce hiring
Responsible (R): Corporate Communications / TA Marketing
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Within 24 hours</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5557_Flow20</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5557_Flow21</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5557_Task10" name="Takedown wave">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Takedown wave: platform reports filed simultaneously on all discovered surfaces via the W3272 machinery (social pages, group chats, marketplaces), registrar action on look-alike domains with IT Security, escalations tracked to closure
Responsible (R): IP Counsel / IT Security
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 1–14 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5557_Flow21</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5557_Flow22</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5557_Task11" name="Victim-guidance desk">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 4: Victim-guidance desk: one standard script — stop paying, report to the platform and the PNP Anti-Cybercrime Group, submit no further personal data, and how to verify any real BuildRight offer; empathy-first, never blame; no ad-hoc commitments of reimbursement
Responsible (R): TA Marketing / Customer Service (W258-class routing)
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: Per episode</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5557_Flow22</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5557_Flow23</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5557_Task12" name="Store &amp; employee briefing">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 5: Store &amp; employee briefing: walk-in script for store staff and HR front desks (where to route victims, what not to say), and an employee advisory so associates recognize and report fresh scam surfaces
Responsible (R): TA Marketing / Store Operations
Accountable (A): VP Store Operations
Duration: 1–2 days</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5557_Flow23</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5557_Flow24</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5557_Task13" name="Law-enforcement referral">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 6: Law-enforcement referral: evidence pack (captures, payment channels, platform metadata, victim count estimate) filed with the PNP Anti-Cybercrime Group; W1337-class coordination where the campaign links to organized fraud
Responsible (R): Corporate Security / IP Counsel
Accountable (A): VP Legal &amp; Compliance
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5557_Flow24</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5557_Flow25</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5557_Task14" name="Verification registry &amp; content hardening">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 7: Verification registry &amp; content hardening: the W3762 portal offer-verification path re-confirmed as the single source of truth; scam patterns folded into candidate-experience FAQ content and onboarding literacy material
Responsible (R): Talent Acquisition Operations / TA Marketing
Accountable (A): TA Marketing / Employer Brand Lead
Duration: 1–2 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5557_Flow25</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5557_Flow26</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W5557_Task15" name="Post-episode review">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 8: Post-episode review: channel monitoring rules tuned (W3764), employer-brand health checked (W3765), recurrence watch left running, and the episode filed as a VS-159 threat-intelligence record
Responsible (R): TA Marketing / Corporate Security
Accountable (A): CHRO
Duration: 2–4 weeks</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W5557_Flow26</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W5557_Flow27</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W5557_End16" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W5557_Flow27</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
      <bpmn:textAnnotation id="W5557_Annotation17">
        <bpmn:text>Controls: - CTL-592 (ensure controlled execution — Employer Brand, EVP &amp; Talent Marketing Strategy (PA-121.1).) | - operational: advisory published within 24 hours of confirmed scam; every takedown, referral, and victim-contact action logged on the case with evidence preserved
Owner: TA Marketing / Employer Brand Lead</bpmn:text>
      </bpmn:textAnnotation>
      <bpmn:association id="W5557_Assoc18" sourceRef="W5557_Annotation17" targetRef="W5557_Start7" associationDirection="None" />
